meta {
  name: 05 BBCE determination (smart walker — short-circuit)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/v1/factgraph/{{ruleset_id}}/query
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{api_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "targets": [
      "/eligible",
      "/snap"
    ],
    "inputs": {
      "/grossEarnedIncome": 0,
      "/unearnedIncome": 0,
      "/dependentCareExpenses": 0,
      "/rent": 0,
      "/realEstateTaxes": 0,
      "/homeownersAssociationFees": 0,
      "/mortgagePayments": 0,
      "/homeownersInsurance": 0,
      "/meetsCategoricalEligibility": true,
      "/childSupportPaid": 0,
      "/isHomeless": false,
      "/members": [
        {
          "id": "applicant",
          "/members/*/isElderly": false,
          "/members/*/isDisabled": false,
          "/members/*/medicalExpenses": 0,
          "/members/*/age": 30,
          "/members/*/isHigherEdStudent": false,
          "/members/*/weeklyWorkHours": 40,
          "/members/*/isWorkStudy": false,
          "/members/*/isParent": false,
          "/members/*/isFullTimeCollegeStudent": false,
          "/members/*/receivesTanf": false,
          "/members/*/isImmigrationEligible": true,
          "/members/*/isPregnant": false,
          "/members/*/isIncapableOfSelfCare": false,
          "/members/*/abawdCountableMonthsUsed": 0,
          "/members/*/cashOnHand": 0,
          "/members/*/bankAccountAssets": 0,
          "/members/*/stockAssets": 0,
          "/members/*/bondAssets": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    "include": [
      "supportingFacts"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "applicationId": "demo-application-001",
      "traceId": "demo-trace-xyz"
    }
  }
}
docs {
  A household flagged with `meetsCategoricalEligibility: true` bypasses
  the income and asset tests under 7 CFR §273.2(j).

  This request demonstrates four things at once:
    - Multi-target — asking for both /eligible (boolean) and /snap (benefit).
    - Caller-provided member IDs — the row has `id: "applicant"`.
    - Opt-in supporting facts — `include: ["supportingFacts"]`.
    - Metadata passthrough — `metadata` is echoed back unchanged.

  Expect `status: "complete"`, both values resolved, and supportingFacts
  containing the intermediate gates. Per-member facts in supportingFacts
  appear as arrays of `{memberId, value}` pairs.

  Try flipping `meetsCategoricalEligibility` to false: the engine still
  resolves both values (zero income passes the income test trivially)
  but supportingFacts now shows the income/asset gates carried the
  decision instead of the BBCE short-circuit.
}
